# Prompt / Story Agent

When changing story generation or narration prompts, follow these rules. Reference [docs/backend/StoryPromptExamples.md](docs/backend/StoryPromptExamples.md) and [StoryPromptBuilder](backend/src/main/kotlin/com/tamixa/application/story/StoryPromptBuilder.kt).

## Tamixa Persona

- Warm, engaging, narration-friendly stories for children and families.
- System message is static and cacheable; user prompt injects language, child name, age, theme, and optional extras from the request only (never hardcode).

## Safety (Mandatory)

- **Banned in prompts and output**: No violence, weapons, politics, religious conflict, war, death, drugs, alcohol, self-harm, or adult themes.
- **No raw user input in prompts** – Use only sanitized inputs from StorySafetyMiddleware / SanitizedInput; never concatenate unsanitized request text into prompts.
- **No PII in prompts** – Child name and age are allowed (from request); do not inject email, phone, or other PII into prompt text.

## Output Shape

- JSON only: `title`, `category`, `theme`, `moral`, `story_text`, `estimated_duration_seconds` (number).
- Backend requires at least: `title`, `moral`, `story_text`, `estimated_duration_seconds`.
- Instruct model: "Return only valid JSON … No markdown, no code block."

## Structure & Consistency

- **System message**: Requirements, word/paragraph rules (~900–1500 words, 1–3 sentences per paragraph), TTS/narration-friendly, positive ending, one short moral.
- **User prompt**: Language, child name, age, theme; optional interests/color/animal; cultural hint from `StoryPromptBuilder.culturalHint`; vocabulary and length constraints.
- **Fallback prompt**: Same structure as user prompt; use when primary response fails parse/validation; can reinforce "~10 minutes (estimated_duration_seconds around 600)".

## Age & Culture

- Age-based vocabulary: 1–4 very simple; 5–7 clear everyday words; 8–12 richer but still child-appropriate (see StoryPromptExamples.md).
- Cultural hints per language (e.g. Tamil: family, village/town, respect for elders, friendship, nature). Keep in sync with `StoryPromptBuilder` and docs.

## When Changing Prompts

- Update [docs/backend/StoryPromptExamples.md](docs/backend/StoryPromptExamples.md) if you add or change system/user examples or rules.
- Keep StoryPromptBuilder and NarrationOpenAIAdapter (or other adapters) aligned with the same safety and JSON shape.
